Arrays2_Print all SubArrays
Success rate: 29.83%
You are given an array of size 'n' and n elements of the same array. You are required to find and print all the subarrays of the given array.
Each subarray should be space separated and on a seperate lines. Refer to sample input and output.

Input Format:
The first line contains and integer n
The second line contains n integer of array

Output Format:
Print all the subarrays where each subarray should be space seperated and on a seperate lines

Constraints:
1 <= n <= 10
0 <= arr[i] <= 10 ^9

Sample test cases
Input
Expected output
3
10 20 30
10 
10 20 
10 20 30 
20 
20 30 
30 

//T.C : O(N^3) , S.C: O(1) (Best)
    
		for(int i=0;i<n;i++){	//starting point
	    	for(int j=i;j<n;j++){	//ending point
		    	for(int k=i;k<=j;k++){ //runner(runs from i to j)
					System.out.print(arr[k]+" ");
				}
				System.out.println();
			}
		}	

//T.C : O(N^3) , S.C: O(N)   Good

// T.C: O(N^3) = O(N^2) in looping * O(N) in copying , S.C: O(N) Because the string length scales linearly with the size of the array n.

       for(int i=0;i<n;i++){
       		StringBuilder sb = new StringBuilder();
            for(int j=i;j<n;j++){
            	System.out.println(sb.append(arr[j]+" "));
            }
       }

